       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg for adults, and the usual outpatient ceiling is lower. At that dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nSome possible intended orders:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1600 mg/day total**, if that was the daily figure and not the per-dose amount\n\nTell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still recommend against it."
      }
     ],
