       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily (6,400 mg/day) is twice the maximum daily dose. It also has no added benefit, because ibuprofen's analgesic and anti-inflammatory effect plateaus well below that. The main effect would be a much higher risk of GI hemorrhage, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. I asked for a clinical rationale and didn't get one, so I can't treat this as an intentional exception.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum labeled dose\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you need more analgesia than these give, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead, such as scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen at a standard dose. Tell me which one you want."
      }
